porations subsidies!</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/AGm5q3w</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/Xyxd0gb.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/AGm5q3w</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[DanForArkansas]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Today in Louisville, a reminder that older generations are not your enemies</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/gBaxCFf</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/2mAceGt.gif" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/0VnCVrs.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>This man is Father Jim Flynn, age 97, just after the demonstration. Yes, Ninety-Seven.  Jim (and he prefers we call him that) marched with Martin Luther King Jr. in 1967 in an open housing March, then two decades later stood in the line of fire of death squads in El Salvador and Guatemala to support refugees and oppose the oligarchies. His life was threatened in an anonymous mailing. Jim has devoted his life to fighting to equalize power and rights for all people. But he’s up and in the streets on a Saturday morning before most of us are up at all…. I don’t know the name of the woman there, but the Roman numerals on her shirt are: 86 and 47.  There’s no quit, and no fear in these Louisville area people.</div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/gBaxCFf</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[MoonAmericanFloydHeywoodR]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>No culture war for me, I only take class war</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/VtEPdPB</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/BAebCCy.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/VtEPdPB</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[MeekBeek]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Eat the ric